While separation should be considered carefully, in many cases, it can be an appropriate solution to persistent unhappiness. You might consider taking some time to explore your options.

Before making any major decisions, remember these important steps:

1) Make sure you have enough resources (savings, employment) to start a new life on your own;

2) Consider seeking counseling for yourself to help process your feelings;

3) Document the reasons why you want separation for legal purposes (e.g., financial protection if he's been irresponsible);

4) Ensure you tell trusted friends about your intentions so they support you afterward.

Many couples benefit from separation as they regain perspective and personal agency. Just make sure to plan your departure tactfully to avoid unnecessary drama.
